      // If percent-decoding fails, keep the text as-is (with + -> space done above)
      // Note: We must re-escape any % that were not valid hex sequences to avoid 
      // accidentally interpreting them later, but since we are returning a plain object 
      // and the spec says "keep that text as it is", we just use the string after + replacement.
      // However, to be safe and consistent with "keep that text as it is", we revert the 
